# Trivy CVE whitelist.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line (e.g. CVE-2024-12345).
# MANDATORY: add a trailing `# exp=YYYY-MM-DD` comment so stale entries are
# caught by a manual audit. Entries without an expiration date should be
# rejected in code review.
#
# Rationale: whitelisting a CVE is an acceptance of risk. It must be temporary
# (fix upstream, bump dep, re-evaluate) and bounded in time.

# Example (remove when no longer needed):
# CVE-2026-4539  # pygments syntax-highlighting | no fix available yet.  exp=2026-07-01

CVE-2026-28390  # libssl3 HIGH dans gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian12 | attente rebuild upstream Google.  exp=2026-05-21
